    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Test methods and lifecycle methods may be declared locally within the current test class, inherited from superclasses, or inherited from interfaces (see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "writing-tests/test-interfaces-and-default-methods.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "writing-tests/test-interfaces-and-default-methods.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). In addition, test methods and lifecycle methods must not be "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "abstract"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and must not return a value (except "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@TestFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods which are required to return a value)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Test classes, test methods, and lifecycle methods are not required to be "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "public"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ", but they must "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "not"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " be "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "private"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "It is generally recommended to omit the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "public"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " modifier for test classes, test methods, and lifecycle methods unless there is a technical reason for doing so – for example, when a test class is extended by a test class in another package. Another technical reason for making classes and methods "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "public"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " is to simplify testing on the module path when using the Java Module System."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Class and method visibility"
              }
            ],
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Fields in test classes are inherited. For example, a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@TempDir"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " field from a superclass will always be applied in a subclass."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Test methods and lifecycle methods are inherited unless they are overridden according to the visibility rules of the Java language. For example, a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Test"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " method from a superclass will always be applied in a subclass unless the subclass explicitly overrides the method. Similarly, if a package-private "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Test"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " method is declared in a superclass that resides in a different package than the subclass, that "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "@Test"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " method will always be applied in the subclass since the subclass cannot override a package-private method from a superclass in a different package."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "See also: "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Field and Method Search Semantics"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "extensions/supported-utilities-in-extensions.html#search-semantics"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Field and method inheritance"
              }
            ],
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following test class demonstrates the use of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Test"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods and all supported lifecycle methods. For further information on runtime semantics, see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "writing-tests/test-execution-order.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "writing-tests/test-execution-order.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Wrapping Behavior of Callbacks"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "extensions/relative-execution-order-of-user-code-and-extensions.html#wrapping-behavior"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
